WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.450
Here's Learn's model, in three parts.

2
00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:04.963
A package says what the
machine should look like.

3
00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:09.263
A policy definition points at that
package by its address and its hash.

4
00:00:09.263 --> 00:00:14.359
And when the definition is assigned, every
machine in scope gets a guest assignment:

5
00:00:14.359 --> 00:00:18.200
the agent downloads the package,
evaluates it and reports back.

6
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.510
Each assignment is one of
three types: audit only,

7
00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:25.400
apply once and report drift,
or apply and keep correcting.

8
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.413
The spelling is case sensitive,
which will matter later.

9
00:00:28.413 --> 00:00:32.014
Custom content for audit and
apply is generally available,

10
00:00:32.014 --> 00:00:34.580
with minimum agent versions on the slide.
